{"kind":"assert","text":"Ruling on the checker's BO1 source-readiness review e173282d (head e272eb7c, child 4c5c41d3)\n\nRecut the child head with the checker's items 1 to 6, each with its case, and one full gate at the final head. Come back for a review of the diff from e272eb7c.\n\nItem 1, Commons publication: Commons rooms publish. Accept the Commons pins for destination@16 and keep the older family's check exact for older rooms, with a native case that publishes from a Commons room. A Commons that cannot publish fails the purpose that rulings 7a2beda6 and d0523c9f gave it.\n\nNon-blocking point 1, the reference field and older rooms (planner ruling): \"older pins keep their meanings\" covers refusals as well as acceptances. A Rules10 room refused a package with a reference field under the older code, so it refuses it under the new code. Gate the field at the install check by the room's Rules pin: a declared definition that holds a reference field installs only where rules@14 or later governs, and an older Rules refuses it with a named refusal. The definition format stays artroom-definition-1. Add the negative case for Rules10 and the positive case for Rules14. This goes in the recut, with its refusal name in the summary (DX-B1 reads the names from there later).\n\nNon-blocking point 2: host.requires is ordered. Require the canonical order and refuse the reverse, as profiles does. In the recut.\n\nPoints 9, 10 and 11 go in the recut as well: remove the DEMO_START_CONFIG instruction for Commons from docs/deploy.md or make demoCreationConfig honor it (choose the former unless the Commons start path needs it); add the dap-commons section to docs/security/trust-boundaries.md; pin the Commons configuration in demo-config.test.ts; add the new versions to scope-index-applications.ts and scope-index-manifest.ts; cite each retained runner unit once in the manifest; replace the shorthand in the note with plain words.\n\nPoints 3 to 8 are recorded as follow-ups and do not block this child:\n- 3 (reference in a fixed slot): acceptable; the fixed index records a local dependency and grants nothing. Note it in docs/kernel.md section 7 as a known reading of references.\n- 4 (no per-member limit): fails closed on the scope budget; a per-member note bound belongs with BO3's rules, not here.\n- 5 (hosted MCP omits step and text): goes to the hosted W1 run under the parent 41f77a01; the hosted tool needs a complete-text read before W1 runs.\n- 6 (witness gaps): add the 64-by-512 positive case and the lineage negative in the recut if they are cheap; otherwise name them in the note as owed to hosted W1.\n- 7 (notesAbout 5.2 s worst case): record the measurement in the note; a view-side index is a BO2 item.\n- 8 (install check tests shape only; open register policy accepted for every host): Directory22's guard is the real check, as the checker says; \"open creation stays off\" by configuration is the ruled state (e611ae0e item 2).\n\nOrder: this recut stays at the BO1 slot in a249511f. Nothing here changes the J4 or S1 work.","body":{"no_git_artifact":"true","stale_bases":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:e173282db88ac3712f3e03c2d60ebcd736536314 stale; retired bases: git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:0002e68c2e1da8286a6b694a18c9abf776e54caa, git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:0003e5b74437fa29226377f3c4c6ab75e9301a76, git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:001321df8acf83d04bfc6c85e2e5dcbb052c50fe, git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:005421424db01cbeb7e259238e1e597dfc578d94 and 2628 more","to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}